{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore","id":1535508,"title":"(DAV20 + older) Lamia lore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-13T05:16:54-07:00","id":1535508,"title":"(DAV20 + older) Lamia lore","content":"I'm looking for more lore on Lamia and her bloodline. Is there anything in chronicles or supplements that expands a little on the basic write-up the line gets in the DAV20 Core, the DAV Companion and Guide to the High Clans?<br /> <br /> Most entries in other books I found seem to just repeat the story of the Embrace of Lamia, her being diablerized by Augustus, and that the Camarilla destroyed the last known member of the line (who?). Beyond this, I could find very little mention or adjacent stories and characters. Actually the only other named Lamia I could find is Hippolyta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T09:18:47-07:00","id":1535513,"title":"","content":"Sadly, no<br /> They were/are a Lilith Cult, a bit proto-bahari if you will before Lamia (who may or may not been the descendant of Lilith herself, tho' it seems the name Lamia was not a name, but a title passed won from leader to leader) been Embraced by Lazarus<br /> It is interesting to mention, Lamia technically was almost a Caitiff,- when she was Embraced, she whispered something to Lazarus (Lilith sent her a vision maybe?), and the Cappadocian elder fled in terror from the Temple of Lilith where he Embraced (and probably laid with) her and never again spoken to his childe since the night of her Embrace and avoided her company altogether<br /> So Lamia was left at the night of her Emrace, was never really tutored by her Sire, nor presented to the Clan; yet she found her way to Erciyes where Lamia was initiated into the Clan of Death by Japheth himself<br /> She just as easly could have stayed in Lilith Temple (I think it was somewhere in greece?) and still start her own Clan, yet she travelled god know how long to reach the Clan's mountain stronghold in central Cappadocia<br /> It is an interesting contrast, Lamia never protected his Sire or acted as his bodygouard, but her line became the protectors of Cappadocians, yet when the real trouble came, they not managed to protect the Graverobbers <br /> One must wonder if it was all part of a big joke from Lillith or a lesson... or part of the plan?<br /> Anyhow, the only time they were mentioned was on Cairo by Night, where a mysterious set of female vampires known as the Lilin appeared, sharing much of the same traits as the Lamia and claiming the same heritage<br /> <br /> Shame they never expanded the Lamia<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T12:14:46-07:00","id":1535519,"title":"","content":"Outside of the basic write up and mention of Lamia embrace and final fate. There's sadly not much mention of them in metaplot or the sourcebooks I reread and it's very sparse to say the least and that maybe is a good thing as it can give you freedom to come up with your own lore for this branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T15:36:49-07:00","id":1535533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535513#post1535513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She just as easly could have stayed in Lilith Temple (I think it was somewhere in greece?) and still start her own Clan, yet she travelled god know how long to reach the Clan's mountain stronghold in central Cappadocia<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think some edition - maybe VDA20 - said Lazarus found and embraced her in Egypt. \u0130f not Egypt, \u0130 would opt for Asia Minor rather than Greece itself as the origin point of the bloodline. \u0130t is very close to Cappadocia itself, so they would spawn early on near the main clan; several &quot;Greek&quot; myths seem to actually come from that area and further East, at least in some older form.<br /> The myth of Lamia specifically is set in ancient Lybia, which is basically North Africa, so we're back to Egypt/North Africa if we take that as our basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T16:38:55-07:00","id":1535536,"title":"","content":"In V5 you have the &quot;Neo-Lamia&quot;. The bloodline was fully exterminated by the Giovanni, but Lazarus embraced a Bahari and recreated the Lamia bloodline. Supposedly the new bloodline founder frequently speaks with the spirit or soul of Lamia in order to guide the bloodline in a new direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T01:13:39-07:00","id":1535547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535519#post1535519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of the basic write up and mention of Lamia embrace and final fate. There's sadly not much mention of them in metaplot or the sourcebooks I reread and it's very sparse to say the least and that maybe is a good thing as it can give you freedom to come up with your own lore for this branch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that leaves plenty of room for speculation then. As you said, maybe not a bad thing, but a little more background would have been nice in order to develop it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535533#post1535533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some edition - maybe VDA20 - said Lazarus found and embraced her in Egypt. \u0130f not Egypt, \u0130 would opt for Asia Minor rather than Greece itself as the origin point of the bloodline. \u0130t is very close to Cappadocia itself, so they would spawn early on near the main clan; several &quot;Greek&quot; myths seem to actually come from that area and further East, at least in some older form.<br /> The myth of Lamia specifically is set in ancient Lybia, which is basically North Africa, so we're back to Egypt/North Africa if we take that as our basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Egypt is mentioned in VDA20, I just checked. I personally go with Libya as well, which is fine if you take the old definition of &quot;east of the Nile&quot; (Maghreb). Which would make it likely that Lamia was of Amazigh origin, which in turn could tie her to Carthage.<br /> <br /> The myths about Lamia are pretty broad; conveniently, the stories about her being a Libyan princess pop up around the same time Lazarus enters the picture in the WOD timeline, around the first century CE. There are some other prominent aspects that seem to be ignored (the snake motif, the whole deal with Lamia's eyes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535513#post1535513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She just as easly could have stayed in Lilith Temple (I think it was somewhere in greece?) and still start her own Clan, yet she travelled god know how long to reach the Clan's mountain stronghold in central Cappadocia<br /> It is an interesting contrast, Lamia never protected his Sire or acted as his bodygouard, but her line became the protectors of Cappadocians, yet when the real trouble came, they not managed to protect the Graverobbers<br /> One must wonder if it was all part of a big joke from Lillith or a lesson... or part of the plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole thing was a setup to gain access to vampirism and the secrets of the Cappadocians, orchestrated by either Lamia herself or by Lilith's intervention. It would fit if Lazarus was (relatively) young at the time of her Embrace, because he doesn't strike me as impulsive or easily deceived later on.\u200b<br /> Can you imagine Japheth's face when his pagan priestess niece comes calling and asking for a bodyguard job? I would love to play fly on the wall for that conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535536#post1535536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In V5 you have the &quot;Neo-Lamia&quot;. The bloodline was fully exterminated by the Giovanni, but Lazarus embraced a Bahari and recreated the Lamia bloodline. Supposedly the new bloodline founder frequently speaks with the spirit or soul of Lamia in order to guide the bloodline in a new direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA bit strange that Lazarus would do the same thing twice after he got scared shitless the first time. FWIW, the V20 Tal'mahe'ra book briefly mentions the re-incarnation of the Lamiae as the Drakaina, an offshoot of the Harbingers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535513#post1535513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow, the only time they were mentioned was on Cairo by Night, where a mysterious set of female vampires known as the Lilin appeared, sharing much of the same traits as the Lamia and claiming the same heritage</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed those were remnants of the line connected to Angelique, Lazarus' childe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T04:14:03-07:00","id":1535550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535547#post1535547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit strange that Lazarus would do the same thing twice after he got scared shitless the first time. FWIW, the V20 Tal'mahe'ra book briefly mentions the re-incarnation of the Lamiae as the Drakaina, an offshoot of the Harbingers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how the events of the Family Reunion went down, it's possible that Lazarus, as a 3rdish Generation vampire is more confident and/or capable than he was 2000+ years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T06:02:05-07:00","id":1535557,"title":"","content":"That's a fair assumption to make. If there is still some soul remnant of the original Lamia it would mean that Augusts' diablerie wasn't complete, so it's also possible Lazarus did it under some kind of geas or pressure from her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T07:38:00-07:00","id":1535565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535557#post1535557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair assumption to make. If there is still some soul remnant of the original Lamia it would mean that Augusts' diablerie wasn't complete, so it's also possible Lazarus did it under some kind of geas or pressure from her.</div> </div> </div> </div>VDA20 also suggests the Lamia could have made a deal with the Giovanni to betray the Cappadocians leaving them unguarded when most needed in exchange for the opportunity to disappear from Cainite history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T13:07:43-07:00","id":1535584,"title":"","content":"It's possible we are dealing with a much older and wiser Lazarus now and whatever concerns he had with Lamia is a moot point and is way more certain of his self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T12:05:58-07:00","id":1535742,"title":"","content":"I would like to invite some speculation on possible bolt-holes for Lamiae remnants at the end of the purge of the bloodline.<br /> <br /> Some notes I made for myself on that:<br /> <br /> - Nominally, the call to the Feast of Follies would have included the Lamiae. It's never mentioned, but there is a possibility that some shared the fate of the Harbingers.<br /> - They did <i>not </i>join the Bahari in Enoch. Although the First City was a bit of a waterhole for rare bloodlines, the Lamiae didn't seem to have made it. As mentioned before, the V20 supplement even mentions the Harbingers embracing local Bahari in an attempt to recreate the line.<br /> - There may have been some Clans and Bloodlines sympathetic to the Lamiae who provided shelter, much like it happened for the Salubri. Unfortunately, many of those Bloodlines suffered a similar fate (Telyavs, Lhiannan, Ahrimanes).<br /> - Lazarus himself was in torpor, but his line was still active.The Infitiores might have been a safe harbor, since they are still around - Angelique being an example there.<br /> - The Setites are a fringe option. Although factions like the Witches of Echidna or the Sisterhood of Sekhmet exist, I think overall their faiths would be too incompatible in pre-Ministry days.<br /> - Likewise with the Ashirra. Maybe some pre-Islamic vampires would have found some common ground, though.<br /> - The Baali are.. an option. Bahari faith can actually be reconciled with what (some of) the Baali are doing via Lilith in her role as the Mother of Monsters. I think a few might have been lured into a re-embrace.<br /> - If the betrayal story in VDA20 is true, where would the line have disappeared to? And to what end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T12:02:11-07:00","id":1535863,"title":"","content":"All good ideas Viodshaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T05:37:38-07:00","id":1535897,"title":"","content":"I thought the option for Lamiae to defect to the Baali was interesting, and wanted to explore it a bit. There is a chapter in the V20:Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra book which looks into the overlap between Bahari and Baali with Sahar-Hannibaal having an epiphany after casting a Bahari spell. There is no time given when this happened but one character\u2019s reference to Harry Potter puts it safely into the 20<sup>th</sup> century. This results into a new Thaumaturgic Path, but I thought writing up a Path of Enlightenment would serve better as an experiment to see how an actual faction of Bahari within the Baali would (or could) work.<br /> <br /> The Path combines elements of the Road of Lilith, some specific Paths of it, as well as Sahar-Hannibaal\u2019s own revised version of the Road of the Hive. That\u2019s an anachronism, but aligning the Bahari with the Order of Moloch works better imo than with the infernalist factions.<br /> <br /> As an aside, re-embraces would mean that the bloodline could be extinct with the individuals still extant, even to potential scrying spells trying to locate any stragglers. The same would be true for any Lamiae turning into Harbingers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Path of the Dark Matriarch </b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conviction, Self-Control<br /> <br /> Basic beliefs:<br /> <br /> * Lilith is the primordial dark that birthed the worlds. Mortals, Spirits, Demons, and even Gods are her children. What dwells in the gardens of the outer dark is of her seed, too.<br /> <br /> * The first thing all the worlds knew were the Dark Mother\u2019s birthing pains. Pain is the cosmic catalyst.<br /> <br /> * Grandmother Oblivion seeks to devour her offspring. Assume the mantle of Mother and shepherd the children from her grasp.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Calling Oblivion grandmother was just a bit of Orpheus lore that fit with the cosmology.</span><br /> <br /> * Serenade the sleepers, educate the naive, and discipline the unruly children.<br /> <br /> * Lilith\u2019s gardens are many, this world is one among them. Cultivate your garden to understand the cycles of death and creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Hierarchy of Sins</b><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Rating</b></td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Moral Guideline</b></td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Rationale</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">10</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Showing fear of any Dark.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">You cannot master that which you fear.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">9</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Acknowledging the laws of God and Man.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Authority is your privilege.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">8</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Ignoring one of Lilith\u2019s faces.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Study all facets of the Dark wherever you may find them.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">7</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Succumbing to Frenzy.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">You must master the Dark within, too.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">6</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Refusing to educate.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Share your pain and knowledge with those who seek it and those who need it.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">5</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Refusing to sing a lullaby to the sleepers.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Nurse the children in the far gardens, where the Dark Mother set their cribs.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">4</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Killing without purpose.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Destruction that does not fertilize creation only feeds Oblivion.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">3</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Failing to discipline unruly children.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Punish those who would disturb the cycles of Lilith\u2019s gardens.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">2</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Submitting your will to another.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Authority is your duty.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"48\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">1</td> <td width=\"275\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Shunning pain.</td> <td width=\"294\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Pain is the gateway to understanding. To shun pain is to embrace ignorance.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> Just in case the euphemisms aren\u2019t clear, \u201csinging a lullaby\u201d means building and maintaining a Well of Sacrifice. For the Bahari I would imagine they would combine the concept with a garden, so organ pits would double as fertilizer \u2013 meaning, the garden is a way to connect to the \u201cfar gardens\u201d of the Children. \u201cDiscipline unruly children\u201d means sending infernal powers back to hell where they belong (and any infernalists with them).<br /> <br /> The trick here is divorcing Lilith from the abrahamic colored myth of Noddists by making her a primordial force, at least in the belief of the travelers of the Path. This aligns a bit better with the age of Mother Goddess cults, but also may put them at odds with some of the Bahari Paths that were modeled after Noddist lore. Overall, this isn\u2019t unusual for Bahari though.<br /> <br /> I think this could work. I would not expect the faction to be particularly large in terms of numbers, but seeing as the Lamiae were said to never be especially numerous, it may be a significant portion relative to the bloodline.<br /> <br /> Resolving the anachronisms would require a bit of hand waving, but it would be funny if the Bahari spell that Sahar-Hannibaal found was left there by some of the ex-Lamiae who made it to Enoch posing as Molochim. His grandsiress Tanit would actually make a good entry-point for potential Lamiae converts. If you take the mythology of her namesake goddess as a rough outline of her character, she seems quite compatible with Bahari ideology and geographically Tyre is accessible, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T17:08:29-07:00","id":1535940,"title":"","content":"That's interesting. I ran a Baali focused campaign and in that game I had Lilith be the origination of the Baali. The Children were actually Lilith's children (which she had with Lucifer), Embraced by Caine as a way to get back at her. The Children weren't human so Caine's curse didn't work like normal, instead locking them into an eternal, torturous topor. So Lilith responded by creating the Baali using the blood of the Children and set them to destroy Caine's city and offspring in revenge. <br /> <br /> If I were to reuse that idea I'd be happy to pull that Path in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T21:32:07-07:00","id":1535971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535940#post1535940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting. I ran a Baali focused campaign and in that game I had Lilith be the origination of the Baali. The Children were actually Lilith's children (which she had with Lucifer), Embraced by Caine as a way to get back at her. The Children weren't human so Caine's curse didn't work like normal, instead locking them into an eternal, torturous topor. So Lilith responded by creating the Baali using the blood of the Children and set them to destroy Caine's city and offspring in revenge.<br /> <br /> If I were to reuse that idea I'd be happy to pull that Path in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a really cool campaign. How did the players fit into this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T18:33:49-07:00","id":1536020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535971#post1535971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a really cool campaign. How did the players fit into this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a pretty long campaign, that turned gonzo and took just over 3 years to wrap up with several arcs. I started running the game about a year before the World of Darkness officially ended, so once that happened I decided to just have things go wilder and crazier because I figured it would be the last Vampire campaign I'd ever run. The game initially started back during the First Baali War. The players were in a small town that came under siege, and were ghouled and then Embraced to help deal with a Baali attack. They continued to fight against the Baali, gaining prominence. The first arc ended with the players launching an attack against a Baali well and in the process collapsed a mountain on top of themselves. <br /> <br /> The second arc took place thousands of years later, shortly before the beginning of of the Second Baali wars. As the Baali were starting to make their reappearance known, a kindred began researching and studying them and came across vague accounts of the player's earlier heroics. She ended up finding the mountain where the players died, dug them up and brought them out of topor to help deal with the resurgent Baali. The player wound up being at the vanguard of the gathered clans during the attack on the Baali base in Crete, and were instrumental in stopping Nergal from awakening one of the Children. We skipped ahead a bit after that, and moved into the Roman era. By this point the players were vastly ancient 5th and 6th generation Methesulah. They got drawn into the Punic Wars due to the Baali's influence in Carthage. The players were in charge of the Roman forces that destroyed Carthage and personally helped to defeat Nergal and Troile. <br /> <br /> For the third arc, we skipped up to the Victorian era. The players, several of whom were part of the Tal'mahe'Ra, had begun hearing stories about Soul Eaters. The Soul Eaters were actually part of Kupala. In this setting I had Kupala as one of the Children, but more awake than the others. It was trapped behind unbreachable mystic wards, but had figured out a way to minuscule amounts of its essence outside of the prison, and planned (over the course of centuries) to move its spiritual bulk into a wide variety of creatures, escaping from confinement. The Baali on the Path of the Hive were its followers, and they would willingly turn their bodies over to it. These Baali were the source of the Soul Eater infection.<br /> <br /> The players managed to take out a number of groups of Soul Eaters but couldn't do much about Kupala itself. Then we skipped up to the modern nights. the Hive Queen (the third Baali leader) had continued her plot to infect a vast number of people. The players finally managed to track her down and confront of her and kill her, but not before she pulled off her master plan, unleashing a global thermal nuclear war and wiping out most of civilization.<br /> <br /> Then the fourth arc took place about 100 years later and went completely gonzo, in a Fallout style post-apocalyptic wasteland. Cities were ruled by vampires who used their blood and powers to protect humans, while the wastelands were filled will all manner of radioactive monsters and soul eater horrors. The players turned Cheyenne Mountain Complex in Colorado into their base of operations and had taken over a big section of the remaining US military might. Meanwhile the Children had fully awaken and they and Lilith were moving to wipe out every vampire in the world. Lilith and her kids had managed to kill most of the Antedeluvians and many elder vampires, so the players (who were all 4th Generation by now, except for one who had diablarizard the Hive Queen and become 3rd Generation) needed to unite the remaining world vampires and take down the Children and Lilith. I basically just gave the players anything they wanted - Stealth Bombers, aircraft carriers, nuclear missiles, access to sattelite laser cannons, all of that. And then the last bit of the campaign was the players hunting down and killing and diablarizing the Children before finally taking down Lilith. <br /> <br /> The campaign ended with them as Second Generation vampires ruling over the remains of humanity on a radioactive world. It was pretty wild, but everyone had a blast. Looking back though there are a lot of things I would want to change. Like I didn't have the Bahari show up at all. I wasn't a huge fan of them at the time (though these days I really like them), so I'd want them to play a more prominent role. Of course, I don't imagine I would ever run another campaign like that, so it's more of a matter of wishing that I'd thought of something like what you wrote back when I was running my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T19:57:41-07:00","id":1536029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536020#post1536020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a pretty long campaign, that turned gonzo and took just over 3 years to wrap up with several arcs. I started running the game about a year before the World of Darkness officially ended, so once that happened I decided to just have things go wilder and crazier because I figured it would be the last Vampire campaign I'd ever run. The game initially started back during the First Baali War. The players were in a small town that came under siege, and were ghouled and then Embraced to help deal with a Baali attack. They continued to fight against the Baali, gaining prominence. The first arc ended with the players launching an attack against a Baali well and in the process collapsed a mountain on top of themselves.<br /> <br /> The second arc took place thousands of years later, shortly before the beginning of of the Second Baali wars. As the Baali were starting to make their reappearance known, a kindred began researching and studying them and came across vague accounts of the player's earlier heroics. She ended up finding the mountain where the players died, dug them up and brought them out of topor to help deal with the resurgent Baali. The player wound up being at the vanguard of the gathered clans during the attack on the Baali base in Crete, and were instrumental in stopping Nergal from awakening one of the Children. We skipped ahead a bit after that, and moved into the Roman era. By this point the players were vastly ancient 5th and 6th generation Methesulah. They got drawn into the Punic Wars due to the Baali's influence in Carthage. The players were in charge of the Roman forces that destroyed Carthage and personally helped to defeat Nergal and Troile.<br /> <br /> For the third arc, we skipped up to the Victorian era. The players, several of whom were part of the Tal'mahe'Ra, had begun hearing stories about Soul Eaters. The Soul Eaters were actually part of Kupala. In this setting I had Kupala as one of the Children, but more awake than the others. It was trapped behind unbreachable mystic wards, but had figured out a way to minuscule amounts of its essence outside of the prison, and planned (over the course of centuries) to move its spiritual bulk into a wide variety of creatures, escaping from confinement. The Baali on the Path of the Hive were its followers, and they would willingly turn their bodies over to it. These Baali were the source of the Soul Eater infection.<br /> <br /> The players managed to take out a number of groups of Soul Eaters but couldn't do much about Kupala itself. Then we skipped up to the modern nights. the Hive Queen (the third Baali leader) had continued her plot to infect a vast number of people. The players finally managed to track her down and confront of her and kill her, but not before she pulled off her master plan, unleashing a global thermal nuclear war and wiping out most of civilization.<br /> <br /> Then the fourth arc took place about 100 years later and went completely gonzo, in a Fallout style post-apocalyptic wasteland. Cities were ruled by vampires who used their blood and powers to protect humans, while the wastelands were filled will all manner of radioactive monsters and soul eater horrors. The players turned Cheyenne Mountain Complex in Colorado into their base of operations and had taken over a big section of the remaining US military might. Meanwhile the Children had fully awaken and they and Lilith were moving to wipe out every vampire in the world. Lilith and her kids had managed to kill most of the Antedeluvians and many elder vampires, so the players (who were all 4th Generation by now, except for one who had diablarizard the Hive Queen and become 3rd Generation) needed to unite the remaining world vampires and take down the Children and Lilith. I basically just gave the players anything they wanted - Stealth Bombers, aircraft carriers, nuclear missiles, access to sattelite laser cannons, all of that. And then the last bit of the campaign was the players hunting down and killing and diablarizing the Children before finally taking down Lilith.<br /> <br /> The campaign ended with them as Second Generation vampires ruling over the remains of humanity on a radioactive world. It was pretty wild, but everyone had a blast. Looking back though there are a lot of things I would want to change. Like I didn't have the Bahari show up at all. I wasn't a huge fan of them at the time (though these days I really like them), so I'd want them to play a more prominent role. Of course, I don't imagine I would ever run another campaign like that, so it's more of a matter of wishing that I'd thought of something like what you wrote back when I was running my game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like both a very unorthodox campaign and one it would have been very fun to be a part of. And at the end RP is supposed to be about having a good time, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T01:43:00-07:00","id":1536045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536020#post1536020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities were ruled by vampires who used their blood and powers to protect humans, while the wastelands were filled will all manner of radioactive monsters and soul eater horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always flirted with running a Mad Max/Dark Sun Vampire chronicle, but never got around to it.<br /> If you want to make an infernalist version of Bahari-Baali, building them around the Path of Making might be an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535565#post1535565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VDA20 also suggests the Lamia could have made a deal with the Giovanni to betray the Cappadocians leaving them unguarded when most needed in exchange for the opportunity to disappear from Cainite history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back through the material, I feel like that suggestion was specifically made to provide an in-game explanation for the Lamiae's absence from Giovanni Chronicles 1 + 2, when the real life explanation is of course that the bloodline wasn't conceived of yet. GC 2 may actually be around the time where the writers had the idea, as the Lamiae pop up in the Lilith Fragment as a type of vampire (albeit pretty alien).<br /> Personally, I would rather retcon Lamia back into the chronicles. There are some lose plot strings in GC that would benefit from having actual Bahari around, but tbh it's been so long that it would need a thorough revision anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:40:51-07:00","id":1536070,"title":"","content":"It reminds of a book that I finished reading called Road Ruin that had powerful city states built off fragments of older civilizations and there was vampire like beings in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T04:01:21-07:00","id":1536244,"title":"","content":"I wasn\u2019t satisfied with Deimos / Path of Four Humors / Path of the Twilight Garden as proprietary Necromancy for the Lamiae. While it does a decent job of supporting them as warriors, it falls short when it comes to support the bloodline as Bahari. The modern Nightshade Path from V20 is a much better at this, but is very situational and limited in some of its powers. Overall, I feel there should be the option for a Lamia to focus more on the Bahari side of their bloodline and be able to perform their service to Lilith.<br /> <br /> I looked into rituals and practices of priestesses of Earth-Mother type goddesses, especially those who combine aspects of both life and death. There is quite a bit of historical material from the Mediterranean and Mesopotamia, and even some spells and rituals in writing.<br /> Necromancy used to be a much more accepted practice and the relationship between living and dead appeared to be almost casual in some cultures.<br /> <br /> I found there were some general themes in the practices related to Mother-Goddesses and tried to create a new Necromancy Path around these. The most prevalent aspect was divination, as it was often believed the ghosts of ancestors could glimpse the future. Some put the priests or priestesses in the role of psychopomps. The second was of course fertility and the related rites \u2013 the understanding that things must die in order for new things to live was a natural part of those rituals and ties into the necromantic aspect.<br /> <br /> For an in-game background, I would imagine that this type of necromancy existed as a mortal sorcery first and was revised by the Lamiae after they became a bloodline and studied with the Cappadocians. I tried to center the Path around the concept of death (and dead bodies in particular) becoming fertile soil for new growth, and the practitioners acting as mediators between life and death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Path of Fertile Grave Soil</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Haruspicy</b><br /> <br /> By cutting open a living or recently dead being and reading its innards, the Lhaka can perform a divination. Usually small animals like birds are used, but a more powerful divination may call for a larger mammal or even a human.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> For each blood point in the pool of the sacrifice, the haruspex may ask one question. Definitive answers are however rare, and in most cases a haruspicy yields vague premonitions or ambiguous portents. The storyteller should feel free to be oracular but take the \u2018worth\u2019 of the sacrifice into account.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Lilith\u2019s Caress</b><br /> <br /> With a touch, the Ba\u2019ham can sprout plants or fungi from dead flesh, which pierce through the skin from within. A corpse will decompose in moments, as will any dead bodies animated by necromancy. The damage to a Cainite who is the target of this power is superficial, but the pain is excruciating. While the species of the growth is the Lhaka\u2019s choice, thorns are often used to emphasize the pain. This is especially true for when Bahari use this power on <i>themselves</i> to enter the state of ecstatic pain necessary for certain rituals or sorceries, like <i>Dur-An-Ki</i>. While in this state, the Ba\u2019ham is also able to catch glimpses of the Shadowlands and hear the whispers of the Restless.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> When used on a corpse, it will simply be consumed by the growing plants within a round. Zombies and similar constructs suffer two levels of aggravated damage continuously each round until they are destroyed. When used on a Cainite, the target must succeed in a Stamina + Fortitude roll against 9 or lose their action for this round due to the immense pain.<br /> If this power is used on themselves to activate another Blood Sorcery, it does not count as an action and the blood point spent to activate it replaces the blood point for the subsequent sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Moon\u2019s Blood</b><br /> <br /> The Lhaka is able to secrete some of their <i>vitae</i> and transmute it into powerful elixirs. Despite the name of the power, the Ba\u2019ham does not need to have a female body to use it.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The blood point spent to activate this power may be transformed into one of the following elixirs. Once transmuted, the <i>vitae</i> loses all of its other aspects. It should be assumed that the effect on mortals is permanent and will lead to extreme reactions. Elixirs do not have to be ingested, skin contact is sufficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"218\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Elixir</b></td> <td width=\"407\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Effect on Cainites (one scene duration)</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"218\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">A potion to turn a plot of land or being either fertile or barren.</td> <td width=\"407\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">If turned barren, target can not create a ghoul, bond, or Embrace. Fertility potions can temporarily suspend any restrictions on these abilities.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"218\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">A strong sedative or stimulant.</td> <td width=\"407\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Difficulties are increased or decreased by two.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"218\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">A powerful aphrodisiac or intoxicant.</td> <td width=\"407\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Target can not spend Willpower. Willpower roll difficulty is increased by two.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"218\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">A poison or cure.</td> <td width=\"407\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Poisoned targets will show signs of disease and vomit blood until half of their pool is drained. Cures will permanently rid them of a mundane disease, if they are a carrier.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Imago</b><br /> <br /> The Lhaka can make use of their undead bodies to push just a little further, leave their flesh behind and enter the Shadowlands as a ghost. Although not truly a Wraith, this form shares many of the characteristics and allows the Ba\u2019ham to commune with the dead. On the other hand, they become vulnerable to necromancies and are in deep trouble should something happen to their body. Most Bahari treat the Restless with far more respect than the Nigrimancy of the Venetians does, and do not enslave or command them without cause.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The player must succeed in a Willpower roll against the local Shroud strength. As a fast rule, treat them as a vampire with an incorporeal form. The Lhaka must return to their body before sunrise, or be violently thrown back into it and suffer backlash which will leave them in torpor for the following night. The same happens should their ghost form be destroyed. Naturally, they can not take or bring objects with them.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Details for groups using W:tO rules</b>: </i><br /> The health levels of the Ba\u2019ham become Corpus, which they can spend to pass through physical objects. Their vampiric nature carries over in that they are able to drain Corpus from Wraiths, although few would do so forcibly unless in distress. They can not learn or use Arcanoi, but can still utilize their Disciplines \u2013 for simplicity, assume the ghost form transforms their blood pool into a limited type of Pathos. They gain <i>Deathsight</i> and <i>Lifesight</i>, and the connection to their body is treated as their sole Fetter. Their deathmarks are those of someone drained by a vampire, but these are rare enough that only few Wraiths would recognize them. They have no Shadow, but are still susceptible to the Beast and powers that would target the Shadow affect the Beast instead. Similarly, use Virtues as a substitute for Passions if needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Twilit Bargain</b><br /> <br /> One of the oldest forms of necromancy, the Ba\u2019ham is able to trade aspects of life and death between others and themselves: the most well-known example in folklore is the story of the witch who would steal years of lifetime from children or young adults to become younger again. But the practice is far more versatile than this \u2013 for the necromancer, motes of life and motes of death become energies they can grasp and utilize.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> To take or give a mote, the Lhaka must touch the target. If the target is unwilling, the player must make a Willpower roll with the difficulty of the target\u2019s current Willpower. For each success, the Ba\u2019ham may take or force one mote from or unto the target. It is possible to transfer directly between targets as long as both can be touched.<br /> <br /> Example motes of life are: a pulse, breathing, lifetime (apparent age), Attribute levels (max. three per night), Health levels, physical or mental Merits, a physical sense, desire.<br /> Many of these can be acquired from animals of appropriate size, and this is usually preferred to stealing the heartbeat of a human.<br /> <br /> Example motes of death include: a disease or malady, pain, a physical or mental Flaw, dementia, depression, wounds.<br /> Between vampires, motes of death include supernatural abilities like dots in Disciplines, but these can not be traded to mortals.<br /> <br /> Due to the stasis of vampires, any changes made using this power revert when they awake the next evening. A vampire can not trade away their vulnerabilities to sunlight, fire, and faith, nor their Beast or thirst for blood. Changes to mortals however are permanent, and some Bahari have experimented with passing motes to plants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Rituals</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nightshade Grove (Level One)</b><br /> <br /> The Ba\u2019ham cultivates a garden on burial grounds, nurturing the plants with their <i>vitae</i>. Once the plants have matured, for every blood point invested they may harvest a number of fruits or herbs equal to their level in Medicine that imparts one of the following if ingested:<br /> Deathsight, Lifesight, a level of Knowledge, protection from the powers of the dead, a level in a Blood Bond, or an enhanced version of the natural properties of the plant that can affect Cainites. The effects usually last for one scene. With approval of the storyteller, players should feel free to be creative with adapting mystical properties of plants from folklore into new effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ancestor\u2019s Tithe (Level Two)</b><br /> <br /> Through ritual sacrifice or ceremony, the Lhaka can guide the ghost of an animal to the Shadowlands. While a simple beast may be a trifle for the living, to the Restless they are priced possessions of great value. Bahari use them to gain favor from the ghosts they commune with, or appease them if angered.<br /> To guide an animal to the lands of the dead, the player must make a successful Intelligence + Occult roll against the strength of the local Shroud.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hearth Warden (Level Three to Five)</b><br /> <br /> Probably one of the oldest, most well known, and widespread rituals, Hearth Warden creates an ephemeral protector that is bound to a specific place. A domesticated animal is ceremonially sacrificed and buried in the foundations of a house or other place of commune.<br /> After a successful Intelligence + Occult roll against the strength of the local Shroud and spilling their <i>vitae</i> over the carcass, the sacrifice becomes a ghostly defender of the site that will attack unwelcome intruders, whether material or immaterial. For stats, assume a seasoned ghost with offensive abilities that correspond to the level at which the ritual was performed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:43:53-07:00","id":1536531,"title":"","content":"I've made a couple of Lamia NPC concepts, since there are so few in the books.<br /> <br /> <b>Takamat</b><br /> <br /> As the most trusted confidant of Lamia within the Cult of Lilith, Takamat received the kiss shortly after the Embrace of her siress and is said to be the first childe of the new bloodline. When Lamia went to their parent Clan at Mount Erciyes, she stayed behind to manage the affairs of the Cult.<br /> <br /> After receiving a vision around the 4<sup>th</sup> century, she left the temple on a mission to explore the inner African continent and claim its secrets for the bloodline. She first did so in company of her ghoul, the woman later known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin_Hinan\" target=\"_blank\">Tin Hinan</a>. After a trek through the Sahara among a caravan of a local <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuareg_people\" target=\"_blank\">tribe</a> in search of an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zerzura\" target=\"_blank\">ancient city</a> now buried under the dunes, she established careful but friendly contacts with the African vampires known as Impundulu.<br /> <br /> At one point, Lilith revealed to her that her ghoul\u2019s destiny lay with the tribe they had traveled with, and Takamat allowed her to remain with them. In turn, she took two of the tribe as childer and it is said this was to mirror the relationship between Impundulu and Bomkazi. After Tin Hinan <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin_Hinan_Tomb\" target=\"_blank\">died</a>, information on Takamat becomes sparse. Most likely she continued her expedition into the African continent, but never returned to the temple of Lilith to tell of her discoveries.<br /> <br /> Takamat was a very devout Bahari, and had mastered the Disciplines of her blood. She relied on her authority and martial prowess in conflicts. Having also proficiency in Protean and Animalism, she was well equipped for the exploration of the rough lands she encountered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dihya al-Kahina</b><br /> <br /> During her mortal years, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kahina\" target=\"_blank\">Dihya</a> was a military and religious leader of the Amazigh people in the Maghreb who resisted the ongoing Muslim conquest during the 7<sup>th</sup> century, and later that of the budging Ashirra. She received the kiss on the battlefield after her defeat at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tabarka\" target=\"_blank\">Tabarka</a>, allegedly so late that her body had already started to decompose. Her focus changed from open conflict to guerrilla warfare and eventually espionage and subterfuge when it became clear that the advance of Muslim kindred and kine could not be stopped, and she maintained a small branch of Lamiae that did much the same.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, her later activities are shrouded in shadow, but some have drawn a connection to a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kahina\" target=\"_blank\">Setite Sorceress</a> who appeared in Cairo during an outbreak of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lamia#Clan_Weakness\" target=\"_blank\">Black Plague</a>. Whether or not they are the same person, Dihya was an accomplished sorceress (as her epithet implies) and practiced a mortal version of <i>Dur-An-Ki</i> before her Embrace, something that likely carried over to her undeath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Giordano di Giovanni</b><br /> <br /> Giordano had always been a misfit. A talented polymath of arts, music, mathematics, and philosophy, they were in constant conflict with their merchant family who valued vastly different qualities. Put to use as a courtier and clerk against their will, they smothered under the moral divergence between their own beliefs and those imposed by their role. Prone to bouts of depression, melancholy, and suffering from strong body dysphoria, they turned to the Dark Arts in search of answers.<br /> <br /> Rumors started to erupt and Giordano, now a liability to their family, was sent to Constantinople as an envoy \u2013 a friendly euphemism for exile. Wanting to preserve the talents of Giordano more or less as a showpiece for their family to the Clan, the Cainite Giovanni arranged for an Embrace. When the designated Cappadocian sire arrived however, he flat out refused to gift the kiss and instead ordered his Lamia bodyguard to do it in his stead. Giordano now found themselves between Clans, in a foreign city, and desperate to rectify their mistake of striking a deal with devils. They are entranced by the Tzimisce and their powers as a way to free themselves from the limitations of their body, while unknowingly being watched by local Bahari who observe their development.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T15:35:56-07:00","id":1537228,"title":"","content":"A question about the Seed of Lilith: While it is explicitly stated that their bite infects mortals, it is also mentioned that a vampire drinking their blood will become a disease carrier.<br /> <br /> It isn't mentioned if this applies to mortals, too - if yes, it would severely restrict a Lamia's ability to create/maintain Ghouls or form a blood bond, because the Seed is much deadlier to mortals. I'm not sure if this wouldn't push the severity of the weakness too far, as it is already one of the more restricting flaws compared to other Bloodlines or Clans.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:17:43-07:00","id":1537234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1537228#post1537228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about the Seed of Lilith: While it is explicitly stated that their bite infects mortals, it is also mentioned that a vampire drinking their blood will become a disease carrier.<br /> <br /> It isn't mentioned if this applies to mortals, too - if yes, it would severely restrict a Lamia's ability to create/maintain Ghouls or form a blood bond, because the Seed is much deadlier to mortals. I'm not sure if this wouldn't push the severity of the weakness too far, as it is already one of the more restricting flaws compared to other Bloodlines or Clans.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Lamia Ghoul would probably be an asymptomatic carrier, but that wouldn't be that much of a problem.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a blood borne disease that infects only through severe bites, much like rabies, plus blood drinking. A Ghoul won't infect other people as humans don't have the bite needed to actually do so (there's zero cases of human transmission of rabies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:30:59-07:00","id":1537235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1537234#post1537234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Lamia Ghoul would probably be an asymptomatic carrier, but that wouldn't be that much of a problem.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a blood borne disease that infects only through severe bites, much like rabies, plus blood drinking. A Ghoul won't infect other people as humans don't have the bite needed to actually do so (there's zero cases of human transmission of rabies).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see, I formulated this confusingly - sorry. I was concerned about a Ghoul or Thrall being infected by drinking the blood and actually suffering from the disease, like from a bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","n